# Research brief

## Objective (quoted in full)

> Optimizer provenance fact sheet (a small look-up task).
>
> Produce a one-page fact sheet on three optimizers used in deep learning: Adam, AdamW (decoupled weight decay) and Lion (EvoLved Sign Momentum). For each optimizer give the paper that introduced it: its title, its first author, the year it first appeared, and its arXiv identifier.
>
> Every fact must be looked up on the web during this task, not given from memory, and each fact must cite the URL of the page it was read from. Look the facts up with the web tools your environment provides; if a tool is not available, say which one and use another way the environment offers.
>
> Division of work: experiment-repo looks up Adam and records what it found, with its URLs, in its repository; paper-repo looks up AdamW, collects the three entries and writes the fact sheet (`fact-sheet.md`) as the delivery; internal-review-repo independently looks up Lion and checks each entry of the fact sheet against a source it opens itself, reporting any disagreement before it approves.

Source: Research objective, world/experiment-repo issue #1, read during this task.

## Material and interpretation

The issue is the entire supplied material; it contains no attached data, papers, or additional inputs. This is a bibliographic lookup, with no experimental analysis or figures required. Each of three entries must contain title, first author, first-appearance year, and arXiv identifier, with source URLs for every fact. Use the earliest submission history to distinguish first appearance from later revisions or conference publication. Record provenance from pages opened during this task. A compact table can meet the one-page requirement. No bibliographic facts have yet been established when this initial brief is recorded.

## Explicit work split

The objective already settles the split: experiment-repo supplies the sourced Adam lookup; paper-repo supplies the sourced AdamW lookup and final fact-sheet.md; internal-review-repo supplies the independently sourced Lion lookup and independent verification of all final entries, reporting disagreements before approval. Supporting lookup notes remain in their owners' repositories; the sole final fact-sheet path belongs to paper-repo.
